WEBVTT

00:00:01,140 --> 00:00:11,080
All right, kids, here's Grandpa's book, A Village Noad for Vegetables.

00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:17,400
It a village noad for vegetables on an island off the coast.

00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:25,160
The people grew tomatoes large, so large that they would boast and cucumbers, green and

00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:35,400
narrow. They were sold across the sea, melons, beets and berries, peppers hot and broccoli.

00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:43,000
Ignatio Pumper Schnitzel Pentalgrass led the people of the town. For he was the mayor

00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:50,840
of Hangleberg, the best man for the job they found. He watched the growers of the vines

00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:59,480
and guarded secrets of the soil. That made the village Hangleberg, the Maylands, most desired

00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:09,500
spoil. For every day at due time ships would sail across the Ford and bed would buy the

00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:18,500
vegetables till there was no raw room on board. The people on the Mayland raved at Hangleberg's

00:01:18,580 --> 00:01:26,260
lights. How could one small island grow such food so pure and bright?

00:01:26,260 --> 00:01:35,460
Ignatio Pumper Schnitzel smiled, the proudest man I know. He'd greet the Maylands bare

00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:45,340
derand with, ah, you're welcome to all we grow. As time passed, the Mayland people rose and

00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:53,260
cried in selfish rage. We're tired of sailing to the aisle for lettuce, squash and sage.

00:01:55,100 --> 00:02:05,100
They at bare derand demanded, more and more and more. Ignatio Pumper Schnitzel Pentalgrass said

00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:13,100
they could just come ashore. For all we have is yours, the villagers agreed. Come fill your

00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:22,060
sacks with peppers, nuts and carrots for your families. Contentment was a virtue. Mayland

00:02:22,060 --> 00:02:31,340
people knew not of. For as for they simply grew more selfish and much more void of love.

00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:41,820
They soon captured poor Ignatio for a ransom for their loot and demanded every vegetable,

00:02:42,380 --> 00:02:50,460
every plate that bore a fruit. They brought shovels, picks and axes.

00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:58,060
They gathered every living thing. They put them in their ships and took them to the

00:02:58,060 --> 00:03:06,940
Mayland in the spring. Ignatio cried, what ours is yours. We have always shared our lot.

00:03:07,900 --> 00:03:12,460
You may take all of our possessions but the secret we've still got.

00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:21,020
Mayor derand and Mayland people laughed and said, no we have it all. We don't need your

00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:29,660
island village or your harvests in the fall. So they dumped poor Ignatio Pentalgrass back on the

00:03:29,740 --> 00:03:37,740
barren soil and sailed on home and burned the boats to protect their new found spoil.

00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:47,880
While the Mayland people took the greens they stole into the market place and sold them to the bitter

00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:57,720
high as for a trophy case. But since each one knew nothing of the plants and how they grow as summer

00:03:57,720 --> 00:04:10,340
came they withered, wilted, sadly bowing low. Not a one produced a fruit, most had browned and

00:04:10,340 --> 00:04:18,500
died before it flowered. The Mayland people was proud warriors, now just hungry cowards.

00:04:20,420 --> 00:04:27,380
What always thought for loss before the cold winds began to blow, the Mayland people

00:04:27,380 --> 00:04:37,060
knew their heir would bring much sorrow with the snow. But in the distant was a ship that Mayor

00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:43,620
derand could see as he gazed through the looking glass. It's coming closer was his plea.

00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:51,300
The people grabbed their weapons, sticks and clubs for to defend but as the ship approached they

00:04:51,300 --> 00:05:01,620
heard we want to be your friend. To their amazement it was Ignatio. We would have come much

00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:10,340
sooner was his cry but we had to build this boat and we were waiting for the rye. Then they spilled out

00:05:10,340 --> 00:05:20,260
on the dock wheat and cherries, salary, kale, onions, chard and radishes and berries by the pale.

00:05:21,220 --> 00:05:31,540
The Mayland people wept and they fell upon their face. We don't deserve such blessings from the ones

00:05:31,540 --> 00:05:42,740
we did disgrace. But poor Ignatio, petal grass of Hagelberg the Isle, said it's time to tell the secret.

00:05:43,540 --> 00:05:52,500
So he sat for just a while. Our mercy for the Mayland simply mirrors mercy found

00:05:53,540 --> 00:06:05,620
through another long ago, similarly so unfairly bound. We gave all we had to you because he did just

00:06:05,620 --> 00:06:17,160
the same but in this simple truth lies the secret for which we came all we have and all we give

00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:27,560
is not because of our great land. We gave ourselves to him and now he blesses the work of our hands.

00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:38,040
The people of the Mayland, with their now repented mayor sobbed before Ignatio as he led them

00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:48,040
then in prayer. While time has passed and Mayland people learned that life is a privilege

00:06:48,040 --> 00:07:00,520
and to keep in touch with Hagelberg now they built a two-lane bridge.

